──[enter-stone] ROOTHOLLOW · STONE OF THE CLIMB · The frontier stands at floor 1
   (Old granite, names lit from within by aether.)
   Handtest — highest floor opened: 1
   The lift opens for everyone when a Warden falls.
   ▣ THE CLIMB AHEAD
   LEVEL 2
     + the Relay Office — letters between climbers — free to write, gold rides along
     + the contract board — 3 world jobs a day — the same three for every climber, paid in gold and XP
     + the night slot — one action a night — rest toward your next kills, or work a shift for coin at dawn
     + new steel on the racks (◈ 130–280) — the next rung of blade, guard and coat — and each cut keen or warded if you'd rather trade upkeep for bite
   FLOOR 2
     + new relics reach the shelves — 1 relic join the racks at floor 2
   LEVEL 3
     + the Arcanum — staves, focuses and caster relics behind the reading door
     + new steel on the racks (◈ 170–370) — the next rung of blade, guard and coat — and each cut keen or warded if you'd rather trade upkeep for bite
     + Cobbled Boots (◈ 500) — +1 speed — the chase, the getaway and the small dodge
   FLOOR 3
     + new relics reach the shelves — 1 relic join the racks at floor 3
   LEVEL 4
     − beginner's mercy ends — a death starts costing gear and a bite of carried gold
     + raise your own banner (◈ 300) — you set the join fee and dues, and steward the store
     + new steel on the racks (◈ 220–510) — the next rung of blade, guard and coat — and each cut keen or warded if you'd rather trade upkeep for bite
   FLOOR 4
     + new relics reach the shelves — 2 relics join the racks at floor 4
   LEVEL 5
     + the fields — ambush other climbers — 3 ⚡ a raid, 2 a day
     …and the tower keeps the rest
   [back] Back to the square

