──[lift] FLOOR 1 · THE FENCEROWS · I · Men — The Fencerows
   Stolen meadowland rolls out under the tower's floodlights. Hedgerows still stand in their old lines, fencing fields no farmer will cut again. Somewhere out in the grass, something is moving.
   "The hedgerows were mine once. Wolves come through the gap in the third hedge — the dogs that kept it are gone. Mind the grass when it stops moving. That's when something has set its feet."
